    "lawSection": "Appropriations",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5967\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act in relation to the implementation of the terms of a written\nagreement between the city university of New York, as a public\nemployer, and its employee organization: international brotherhood of\nteamsters local 237; and making appropriations therefor\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThis bill would implement the terms of a collective bargaining\nagreement between the City University of New York (CUNY), as a public\nemployer, and its employee organization: the International Brotherhood\nof Teamsters Local 237 (IBT 237).\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 of this bill would authorize CUNY to implement the terms of\nthe written collective bargaining agreement with IBT 23tin effect for\nthe period from August 18,2006 through September 17, 2009.\n\nSection 2 of this bill would provide that the salary increases and\nbenefit modifications authorized under section 1 of the bill would be\nimplemented contingent upon certification by the CUNY Chancellor, the\nCommissioner of the New York City Office of Labor Relations and the\nDirector of the New York State Governor's Office of Employee Relations\nto the State Director of the Budget and State Comptroller that such\ncollective bargaining agreement has been fully executed and ratified\nby bargaining unit members and approved by the CUNY board of trustees.\n\nSection 3 of this bill appropriates $5,330,000 to the credit of CUNY's\nFiduciary Fund for expenses already accrued, or to accrue after July\n1, 2006, to implement the terms of the agreement described in section\n1 of this bill.\n\nSection 4 of this bill appropriates $4.6 million out of moneys in the\nGeneral Fund to the credit of the local assistance account to support\nthe salary increases and benefit modifications authorized through the\nend of the 2008-09 academic year.\n\nSection 5 of the bill provides that it would be effective immediately\nand be deemed to have been in full force and effect upon approval of\nthe collective bargaining agreement by the CUNY Board of Trustees and\nupon ratification of such agreement by the employee organization.\n\n EXISTING LAW :\n\nChapter 135 of the Laws of2005 implemented the terms of the agreement\nbetween CUNY and IBT 237 for the period July 1,2002 through June 30,\n2006.\n\n STATEMENT IN SUPPORT :\n\nThis bill is necessary to implement the collective bargaining\nagreement between CUNY and IBT 237 in effect for the period from\nAugust 18, 2006 through September 17, 2009. It would ensure the\npayment of negotiated salary increases and other aspects of such\ncollective bargaining agreement between the parties.\n\n BUDGET IMPLICATIONS :\n\nThis bill includes a $5.3 million Fiduciary Fund appropriation and a\n$4.6 million General Fund Aid to Localities appropriation to support\nthe retroactive and current year costs of salary increases and benefit\nmodifications included in the collective bargaining agreement for the\nperiod August 18, 2006 through September 17, 2009. The General Fund\nAid to Localities appropriation reimburses the City University of New\nYork for pre-financing these costs.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis bill would take effect immediately and would be deemed to have\nbeen in full force and effect upon approval of the written agreement\nby the board of trustees of CUNY and upon ratification of the written\nagreement by the employee organization.\n",
